<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Jordanian airliner in emergency Irish landing.</title>
<headline>Jordanian airliner in emergency Irish landing.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Royal Jordanian airliner with 162 people on board was forced to make an emergency landing at Ireland's Shannon airport on Sunday after developing mechanical problems, airport officials said.</p>
<p>Some reports said the Jordanian Prime Minister Abdul-Karim al-Kabariti was on board but this could not immediately be confirmed. The plane was on a flight from New York to the Jordanian capital, Amman.</p>
<p>Ambulances and fire engines were deployed when the aircraft touched down but there were no incidents.</p>
</text>
